## raylibx/shapes3d.pengu
## Layer-2 wrapper over the 21 primitive 3D shape functions of the `raylib` binding.
##
## The family splits by the anchor rule of `docs/plans/raylibx.md` D9, extended to 3D:
## raylib marks the functions whose first argument *is* the anchor with a `V` in the name.
##
## - **4 methods on `raylib.Vector3`**: `draw_point`, `draw_cube`, `draw_cube_wires`,
##   `draw_plane`. Each drops the binding's `_v` suffix, so `pos.draw_cube with extent, color`
##   reads as "at `pos`, draw a cube of `size`".
## - **17 module-level functions**: everything else, with the binding's exact names. The
##   sphere and cylinder families take a `Vector3` centre but carry no `V`, so they stay
##   here; making them methods would invent names that no longer say which C function runs.
##
## This is family `shapes3d` of `raylibx`; see `docs/plans/raylibx_shapes3d.md`.
##
## ## Drawing needs a 3D mode
## Every entry issues a raylib drawing command and is only meaningful between `BeginMode3D`
## and `EndMode3D`. The tests assert only the empty-slice guard of `draw_triangle_strip_3d`;
## the rest of the surface is type-checked by `draw_api_probe` and not called in CI.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation and nothing to release. The only FFI boundary is `slice of Vector3` ->
## `ref to void` in `draw_triangle_strip_3d`, which guards the empty slice before taking
## the address of element zero.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## import raylib
## import raylibx_shapes3d
##
## weave main into int:
##     var center as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 0.0, y is 1.0, z is 0.0
##     calling center.draw_cube with (with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 1.0), raylib.GREEN
##     calling draw_grid with 10, 1.0
##     return 0
## ```


import raylib
import std.ffi
import std.ward

enchanting raylib.Vector3:

    ## Sets a single 3D point at this position.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `color`: the point colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## calling pos.draw_point with raylib.RED
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation; a single direct C call.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## Nothing; a one-pixel point is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ## ```

    weave draw_point with color as raylib.Color into void:
        calling raylib.DrawPoint3D with (essence of self), color

    ## Draws a filled cube centred on this point.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `extent`: the width, height and length of the cube.
    ## - `color`: the fill colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## calling center.draw_cube with (with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 1.0), raylib.GREEN
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation; a single direct C call.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## Nothing; the cube is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ## ```

    weave draw_cube with extent as raylib.Vector3, color as raylib.Color into void:
        calling raylib.DrawCubeV with (essence of self), extent, color

    ## Draws the wireframe of a cube centred on this point.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `extent`: the width, height and length of the cube.
    ## - `color`: the wire colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## calling center.draw_cube_wires with (with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 1.0), raylib.WHITE
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation; a single direct C call.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## Nothing; the wireframe is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ## ```

    weave draw_cube_wires with extent as raylib.Vector3, color as raylib.Color into void:
        calling raylib.DrawCubeWiresV with (essence of self), extent, color

    ## Draws a filled plane centred on this point.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `extent`: the plane's width and length in world units, as a `Vector2`.
    ## - `color`: the fill colour.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
    ## calling center.draw_plane with (with x is 10.0, y is 10.0), raylib.LIGHTGRAY
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## No allocation; a single direct C call.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## Nothing; the plane is drawn into the current 3D frame.
    ## ```

    weave draw_plane with extent as raylib.Vector2, color as raylib.Color into void:
        calling raylib.DrawPlane with (essence of self), extent, color

