## ```pengu
## calling draw_circle_3d with center, 1.0, (with x is 0.0, y is 1.0, z is 0.0), 90.0, raylib.RED
## ```

weave draw_circle_3d with center as raylib.Vector3, radius as f32, rotation_axis as raylib.Vector3, rotation_angle as f32, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawCircle3D with center, radius, rotation_axis, rotation_angle, color

## Draws a filled 3D triangle.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `v1`, `v2`, `v3`: the triangle vertices.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_triangle_3d with a, b, c, raylib.RED
## ```

weave draw_triangle_3d with v1 as raylib.Vector3, v2 as raylib.Vector3, v3 as raylib.Vector3, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawTriangle3D with v1, v2, v3, color

## Draws a filled triangle strip through a list of points.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `points`: the strip vertices, in order.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## An empty `points` slice draws nothing and is not an error: the guard exists because taking the address of element zero of an empty slice is out of bounds.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_triangle_strip_3d with (points at 0 to 3), raylib.BLUE
## ```

weave draw_triangle_strip_3d with points as slice of raylib.Vector3, color as raylib.Color into void:
    if (points.length) == 0:
        return
    let raw as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (points at 0)) to (ref to void)
    calling raylib.DrawTriangleStrip3D with raw, (points.length), color

## Draws a filled cube from separate dimensions.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `position`: the cube **centre**.
## - `width`, `height`, `length`: the size along each axis.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## The vector method `draw_cube` wraps `DrawCubeV` instead; both take a `Vector3` centre, but this one takes the three dimensions separately. They differ only in the C function, which is why both names exist.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_cube with center, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, raylib.GREEN
## ```

weave draw_cube with position as raylib.Vector3, width as f32, height as f32, length as f32, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawCube with position, width, height, length, color

