## Draws a filled sphere.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `center`: the sphere centre.
## - `radius`: the sphere radius.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## This stays a free function even though its first argument is the natural subject: raylib has no `DrawSphereV`, so there is no `V` name to key the anchor rule on (see the family plan D3).
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_sphere with center, 1.0, raylib.BLUE
## ```

weave draw_sphere with center as raylib.Vector3, radius as f32, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawSphere with center, radius, color

