## Draws a filled cylinder with its base centre at a position.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `position`: the **base** centre.
## - `radius_top`, `radius_bottom`: the radii at each end; different values give a cone or a truncated cone.
## - `height`: the cylinder height.
## - `sides`: the number of sides.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## `position` is the **base**, not the centre of mass: the cylinder extends upwards from it.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_cylinder with pos, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 12, raylib.PURPLE
## ```

weave draw_cylinder with position as raylib.Vector3, radius_top as f32, radius_bottom as f32, height as f32, sides as int, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawCylinder with position, radius_top, radius_bottom, height, sides, color

## Draws a filled cylinder between two points.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `start`, `end`: the two end centres.
## - `start_radius`, `end_radius`: the radius at each end.
## - `sides`: the number of sides.
## - `color`: the fill colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## Two equally good anchors, so this is not a method: which end would be the receiver?
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_cylinder_ex with a, b, 1.0, 0.5, 12, raylib.PURPLE
## ```

weave draw_cylinder_ex with start as raylib.Vector3, end as raylib.Vector3, start_radius as f32, end_radius as f32, sides as int, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawCylinderEx with start, end, start_radius, end_radius, sides, color

