## Draws a ray as a line from its origin along its direction.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `ray`: the ray to draw, as `raylib.Ray` (`position` plus `direction`).
## - `color`: the line colour.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## Kept as a free function rather than a `Ray` method: `Ray` has no other wrapper methods and no row in the master plan's registry, so giving it one method would be a registry decision rather than a family one.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_ray with ray, raylib.RED
## ```

weave draw_ray with ray as raylib.Ray, color as raylib.Color into void:
    calling raylib.DrawRay with ray, color

## Draws a ground grid on the world XZ plane.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `slices`: the number of lines to draw in each direction.
## - `spacing`: the distance between lines in world units.
##
## ## Returns
## Nothing; the shape is drawn into the current 3D frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Requires an active 3D drawing frame (`BeginMode3D`/`EndMode3D`). Calling it outside one is undefined by raylib.
## The only function in the family that takes no colour: it uses raylib's own grid colour.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation; a single direct C call.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling draw_grid with 10, 1.0
## ```

weave draw_grid with slices as int, spacing as f32 into void:
    calling raylib.DrawGrid with slices, spacing

# --- Tests ---

test "draw_triangle_strip_3d on an empty slice is a no-op":
    var empty as list of raylib.Vector3 is list of raylib.Vector3
    defer banish empty
    calling draw_triangle_strip_3d with (empty at 0 to 0), raylib.RED

# The whole family is window-bound: every entry below issues a raylib drawing command
# that is only meaningful between BeginMode3D and EndMode3D, so none of it is asserted
# in CI. This probe exists so that every public signature is type-checked at build time.
weave draw_api_probe into void:
    var a as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 0.0, y is 0.0, z is 0.0
    var b as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 1.0, y is 0.0, z is 0.0
    var c as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 0.0
    var d as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 1.0
    var box as raylib.Vector3 is with x is 1.0, y is 1.0, z is 1.0
    var flat as raylib.Vector2 is with x is 10.0, y is 10.0
    var col as raylib.Color is raylib.RED
    var strip as list of raylib.Vector3 is list of raylib.Vector3
    defer banish strip
    var ray as raylib.Ray is with position is (with x is 0.0, y is 0.0, z is 0.0), direction is (with x is 0.0, y is 1.0, z is 0.0)
    calling a.draw_point with col
    calling a.draw_cube with box, col
    calling a.draw_cube_wires with box, col
    calling a.draw_plane with flat, col
    calling draw_line_3d with a, b, col
    calling draw_circle_3d with a, 1.0, (with x is 0.0, y is 1.0, z is 0.0), 90.0, col
    calling draw_triangle_3d with a, b, c, col
    calling draw_triangle_strip_3d with (strip at 0 to 0), col
    calling draw_cube with a, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, col
    calling draw_cube_wires with a, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, col
    calling draw_sphere with a, 1.0, col
    calling draw_sphere_ex with a, 1.0, 8, 8, col
    calling draw_sphere_wires with a, 1.0, 8, 8, col
    calling draw_cylinder with a, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 12, col
    calling draw_cylinder_ex with a, b, 1.0, 0.5, 12, col
    calling draw_cylinder_wires with a, 1.0, 1.0, 2.0, 12, col
    calling draw_cylinder_wires_ex with a, b, 1.0, 0.5, 12, col
    calling draw_capsule with a, b, 0.5, 8, 8, col
    calling draw_capsule_wires with a, b, 0.5, 8, 8, col
    calling draw_ray with ray, col
    calling draw_grid with 10, 1.0
